# Frame and overlays: Opacity paints a positioned box, with everything it contains, faint over what lies beneath.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Frame and overlays · Opacity
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: disc
			Box:
				Width: 90
				Height: 90
				Corner radius: 50%
				Background: accent
	Section:
		Text: Frame and overlays
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Opacity
		Paragraph: `Opacity` goes from `0%` (nothing is seen) to `100%` (opaque). The whole box is made faint as one piece: two boxes that overlap inside it do not show through each other. It only changes how the box is painted, never the layout.
			Style: intro
		Text: Overlay without Opacity, with Opacity: 60% and with Opacity: 25%
